---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import GradientDivider from "../../components/GradientDivider.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Markly Terms of Service"
  description="Terms of Service for the Markly link saving and bookmark application."
>
  <main class="home-page">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title">Markly Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="hero-text">Last updated: September 2026</p>
    </section>

    <GradientDivider />

    <section class="policy-grid">
      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Agreement to These Terms</h2>

        <p>
          These Terms of Service govern your access to and use of Markly, a
          Voxiverse application designed to help you save, organize, manage,
          annotate, and return to links and bookmarks.
        </p>

        <p>
          By downloading, accessing, or using Markly, you agree to these Terms.
          If you do not agree with these Terms, you should discontinue use of
          Markly.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Using Markly</h2>

        <p>
          Markly provides tools for saving and organizing links and related
          information. Features may include bookmarks, folders, tags, notes,
          favorites, pinned items, archived items, collections, activity
          information, and other organizational tools.
        </p>

        <p>
          You are responsible for how you use Markly and for the links,
          descriptions, notes, tags, collection names, and other content you
          choose to save or create within the application.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Your Content</h2>

        <p>
          You retain ownership of the original information and content you add
          to Markly, including your saved links, notes, tags, folder names,
          collection names, and other information you create within the app.
        </p>

        <p>
          By using Markly, you permit the application to store, process, display,
          organize, and synchronize that information as necessary to provide
          Markly's functionality.
        </p>

        <p>
          Voxiverse does not claim ownership of the content you save or create
          in Markly merely because you use the application.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Saved Websites & External Content</h2>

        <p>
          Markly allows you to save links to websites, pages, articles, media,
          services, and other content operated or published by third parties.
          Saving a link in Markly does not mean that Voxiverse owns, controls,
          endorses, or is affiliated with the linked content.
        </p>

        <p>
          Third-party websites may change, move, restrict access, become
          unavailable, or remove content at any time. Voxiverse cannot guarantee
          that a saved link will remain available or that the content located at
          that link will remain unchanged.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Third-Party Terms</h2>

        <p>
          When you open or interact with a third-party website or service through
          a link saved in Markly, your use of that website or service is governed
          by its own terms, policies, and rules.
        </p>

        <p>
          Voxiverse is not responsible for the content, availability, security,
          accuracy, privacy practices, or conduct of third-party websites and
          services.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Accounts & Sign In</h2>

        <p>
          Certain Markly features may allow or require you to sign in to an
          account. Markly currently supports Sign in with Apple for account
          authentication and cross-device synchronization.
        </p>

        <p>
          You are responsible for maintaining access to the Apple account and
          device credentials associated with your Markly account. You should not
          attempt to access another person's account or impersonate another user.
        </p>

        <p>
          Authentication services provided by Apple are also subject to Apple's
          own terms, policies, and availability.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Synchronization</h2>

        <p>
          Markly may provide synchronization features that allow your Markly data
          to remain available across supported devices when you are signed in.
        </p>

        <p>
          Synchronization can depend on internet connectivity, account status,
          device availability, third-party infrastructure, and other technical
          conditions. Continuous or uninterrupted synchronization cannot be
          guaranteed.
        </p>

        <p>
          You remain responsible for reviewing important information and
          maintaining any separate copies you consider necessary.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Acceptable Use</h2>

        <p>
          You may use Markly for lawful personal and organizational purposes. You
          may not use Markly in a way that violates applicable law, infringes the
          rights of another person, interferes with the operation of the
          application, or attempts to gain unauthorized access to Voxiverse
          systems or services.
        </p>

        <p>
          You may not attempt to disrupt Markly, bypass security measures, abuse
          connected services, distribute malicious content through Voxiverse
          systems, or use the application as part of unlawful or fraudulent
          activity.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Copyright & Intellectual Property</h2>

        <p>
          Markly, including its software, interface, design, branding, graphics,
          original components, documentation, and other Voxiverse-created
          materials, is owned by Voxiverse or its respective rights holders and
          is protected by applicable intellectual property laws.
        </p>

        <p>
          These Terms do not transfer ownership of Markly or Voxiverse
          intellectual property to you. You are granted a limited right to use
          the application for its intended purpose while these Terms remain in
          effect.
        </p>

        <p>
          Content available through websites you save in Markly remains subject
          to the intellectual property rights of its respective owners.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Availability & Changes</h2>

        <p>
          Markly may be updated, changed, expanded, redesigned, or modified over
          time. Features may be added, altered, temporarily unavailable, or
          removed as the application develops.
        </p>

        <p>
          Voxiverse does not guarantee that every feature will remain available
          permanently or that Markly will operate without interruptions, delays,
          bugs, or compatibility issues.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Beta & Developing Features</h2>

        <p>
          Some Markly features may occasionally be introduced, tested, or
          provided while still under active development.
        </p>

        <p>
          Features under testing may contain bugs, behave unexpectedly, change
          substantially, or be removed. Feedback submitted about these features
          may be used to investigate problems and improve Markly.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Feedback & Reports</h2>

        <p>
          Markly may provide ways for you to submit bug reports, feature
          requests, ideas, beta feedback, attachments, or other reports to
          Voxiverse.
        </p>

        <p>
          Information you intentionally submit through these systems may be used
          to review your report, investigate technical issues, communicate about
          the report, improve Markly, and maintain Voxiverse support and
          development records.
        </p>

        <p>
          Submitting an idea or feature request does not create an obligation for
          Voxiverse to implement, publish, compensate, or provide attribution for
          that suggestion.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>No Guarantee of External Content</h2>

        <p>
          Markly helps you organize access to content on the web, but it does not
          control that content. Voxiverse does not guarantee that information
          found through a saved link is accurate, complete, safe, current, or
          appropriate for your needs.
        </p>

        <p>
          You are responsible for deciding whether to visit, rely on, download
          from, purchase from, or otherwise interact with any website you access
          through a saved bookmark.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Data Loss</h2>

        <p>
          Reasonable care is taken in developing and maintaining Markly, but no
          software or data-storage system can guarantee against every possible
          error, device failure, synchronization problem, corrupted record,
          service interruption, or accidental deletion.
        </p>

        <p>
          You should maintain independent copies of information that is
          especially important to you when appropriate.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>

        <p>
          Markly is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis to the extent
          permitted by applicable law.
        </p>

        <p>
          Voxiverse does not guarantee that Markly will always be uninterrupted,
          error-free, compatible with every device or service, or that every
          third-party link, preview, piece of metadata, or external resource will
          remain available.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Limitation of Liability</h2>

        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, Voxiverse will not
          be liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or similar
          damages resulting from your use of Markly or your inability to use the
          application.
        </p>

        <p>
          This includes losses related to unavailable third-party websites,
          deleted or unavailable bookmarks, synchronization interruptions,
          external content, service outages, or reliance on information obtained
          from a linked website.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Suspension or Termination</h2>

        <p>
          Access to certain Markly or Voxiverse services may be restricted or
          terminated when necessary to protect the application, its users, its
          infrastructure, or Voxiverse from abuse, unlawful activity, security
          threats, or serious violations of these Terms.
        </p>

        <p>
          You may stop using Markly at any time.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Privacy</h2>

        <p>
          Your use of Markly is also subject to the Markly Privacy Policy, which
          explains how information associated with the application is handled.
        </p>

        <p>
          The Privacy Policy should be reviewed alongside these Terms because
          both documents apply to your use of Markly.
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href="/legal/markly/privacy" class="policy-link">
            View Markly Privacy Policy
          </a>
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Changes to These Terms</h2>

        <p>
          These Terms may be updated from time to time to reflect changes to
          Markly, Voxiverse services, legal requirements, or the way features are
          provided.
        </p>

        <p>
          When these Terms are updated, the revised version will be published on
          this page and the last updated date will be changed accordingly.
          Continued use of Markly after updated Terms become effective
          constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms where permitted by law.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Severability</h2>

        <p>
          If any provision of these Terms is found to be invalid or
          unenforceable, the remaining provisions will continue to apply to the
          fullest extent permitted by law.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Contact</h2>

        <p>
          If you have questions about these Terms of Service or about Markly,
          you can contact Voxiverse.
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href="/contact" class="contact-button">Contact</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .policy-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding-bottom: 5rem;
  }

  .policy-card {
    background: var(--surface-standard);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 24px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .policy-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .policy-card h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--heading-small);
  }

  .policy-card p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .policy-card a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .policy-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    color: var(--accent-periwinkle) !important;
  }

  .policy-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .contact-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
    color: var(--color-bg);
    border: 1px solid rgba(242, 239, 231, 0.12);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .contact-button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .policy-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .policy-card {
      padding: 1.25rem;
      border-radius: 20px;
    }
  }
</style>